.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt NOVI-LIVE-DESKTOP 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm novi-live-desktop
.Nd bring up the desktop on a live boot
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The base image is console-only: the desktop is packages, and the
installation medium carries the whole signed repository.
A live boot that wants a desktop therefore
.Em installs
one \(em into the tmpfs overlay, from a directory on the medium, with
the same signature and hash checks a network install gets.
It takes a couple of seconds, and it is the architecture
demonstrating itself rather than being described.
.Pp
.Nm
is run from
.Pa /etc/s6-linux-init/scripts/rc.init
when
.Va novi.live.desktop
is on the kernel command line, which the medium's
.Dq Live Desktop
menu entry passes.
.Pp
It syncs the index, installs
.Sy novi-desktop ,
and then
.Em declares
what it did:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
novi-state set packages.novi-desktop present
novi-state set services.seatd on
novi-state set services.novi-shell on
novi-state boot
.Ed
.Pp
Declaring rather than merely starting is the point:
.Nm novi-state diff
on a live session should say the machine matches its document, and
the document should say a desktop is what this boot is.
.Ss Everything here is best-effort
This runs during boot, and a live session that could not fetch a
desktop should still get a login prompt.
So every failure is a message and an exit 0, never a boot that stops.
.Pp
Messages go to the console as well as to stderr.
stderr is the s6 catch-all logger, which is right for a record and
wrong for a person:
.Pa rc.init
runs this
.Em after
the gettys are up, so a live user is already looking at a login
prompt while it works, and the screen would otherwise flip to a
compositor with no explanation.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "NOVI_LIVE_REPO" -compact
.It Ev NOVI_LIVE_REPO
The repository to install from.
Default
.Pa /run/live/novi-repo .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/run/live/novi-repo" -compact
.It Pa /run/live/novi-repo
The signed repository on the live medium.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
Always 0.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr novi-install 1 ,
.Xr novi-state 1 ,
.Xr pkg 1 ,
.Xr system.conf 5
.Sh STANDARDS
RFC 0007.
.Sh CAVEATS
The plain console menu entry does
.Em not
run this, so it never syncs the on-medium index \(em and
.Nm pkg install
there answers
.Dq Package not found
about a medium that is carrying the package.
Run
.Nm pkg sync
first on a console live boot.
.Pp
Because every step here ends in a fallback, the final
.Dq desktop ready
is printed whatever happened before it.
It means this script finished, not that a compositor is on screen.
